  "notes": [
    "Cambodia/Kampuchea and Myanmar/Burma share the same common Chinese names. Their alternate English forms remain in parentheses so the source aliases are not silently discarded.",
    "Belarus/Byelorussia share the same common Chinese name. The alternate English form remains in parentheses rather than introducing a distinct polity or using the ambiguous shorthand 白俄.",
    "Kamerun reuses the catalog's 德属喀麦隆 translation for the source's historical territorial name; this is a name translation, not a record association.",
    "Inini is deliberately left untranslated: searches returned the same spelling for a river and virus, which do not establish a sufficiently reliable Chinese territorial name.",
    "Existing catalog labels for Dominican Republic and German Democratic Republic were made more explicit as 多米尼加共和国 and 民主德国; this avoids an abbreviation in a source-name glossary.",
    "The COW source contains 273 distinct cntry_name values across 805 features. Yugoslavia/Serbia replaces the former source key Yugoslavia; the slash qualifier is retained.",
    "The source name Congo is intentionally translated as 刚果, while Congo, Democratic Republic of (Zaire) retains 民主共和国 and 扎伊尔. Congo includes both colonial and sovereign records; appending 共和国 to every Congo label would mislabel its colonial periods.",
    "Sudan and South Sudan remain distinct as 苏丹 and 南苏丹. Source Sudan records include a colonial period, so no timeless republican, Anglo-Egyptian, or modern territorial qualifier is added.",
    "Guinea, Guinea-Bissau, Equatorial Guinea, Papua New Guinea, New Guinea (German New Guinea) (Kaiser Wilhelmsland), and West Irian (Dutch New Guinea) retain each source qualifier. Guinea includes French-colonial and sovereign periods, so its translation 几内亚 is not replaced by a timeless 法属几内亚 label.",
    "Micronesia (Federated states of) is rendered as 密克罗尼西亚联邦, incorporating the parenthetical constitutional qualifier into the natural Chinese word order. Dominica 多米尼克 remains distinct from Dominican Republic 多米尼加共和国."
  ],
